            <div class="step2-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Unique Contribution</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-1.png">
                <p>The Jester Archetype is one of the three archetypes who desire nothing more but to connect with others and enjoy life.It's this taste for joy that is the Jesters&rsquo; unique contribution to the world, and also how The Jester Archetype makes sense of the world.To the Jester, life is not worth living if you can&rsquo;t have fun and it&rsquo;s not possible to connect with others if you don&rsquo;t enjoy the experience of connecting.</p>
                <p>Jesters do not yearn for intimacy like the Lover as a form of connection, nor do they seek connection through attaining a sense of belonging like the Member archetype.To the Jester, entertaining, having fun and enjoying life is the only way to do things.</p>
                <p><strong>Life&rsquo;s A Party</strong></p>
                <p>True to their beliefs, Jesters are almost always known for bringing fun and laughter to whatever social occasion they are at and are probably one of the most popular archetypes - at first glance.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s safe to say that the Jester is committed to a fault to their plight.However, as admirable and dedicated that might sound it doesn&rsquo;t always serve them well - as we will come to see.</p>
                <p>Life is one big party, at least it would be if the Jester had anything to do with it.The trouble is, the Jester has to learn that life cannot always be a party.There are times when too much frivolity can become too much, or even inappropriate.It can also serve as a distraction too which can sabotage the Jesters dreams.</p>
                <p>Let's remember that the Jesters primary focus is to connect through enjoyment. But if that enjoyment becomes too superficial, then the Jester will not experience the joy that he or she seeks - especially if the superficial fun doesn&rsquo;t allow the Jester to meet their innate needs and attain a sense of fulfillment.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This approach also does not support the Jester in making sound connections; instead the Jester starts to become dull and annoying to others (and even to themselves). As a result, as much as the Jester will be able to put a smile on their face and joke away their troubles, they can start to cry inside.And, well, if the Jester is crying inside, they are certainly not enjoying life on the outside.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s the Jesters job to understand this quirk so that they might find a way to balance it out.And if you are a Jester, you are in good hands because we are about to show you how.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Keep walking with us, and in no time at all, you&rsquo;ll be smiling from the inside out, and the outside in. Everybody will come to love you for who you are for you are about to become incredible company if you choose to take this walk.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>As you start to read on, you&rsquo;ll learn how, despite the Jester&rsquo;s ability to bring sunshine and laughter to even the darkest situations, they also have some severe challenges that they have to overcome so that they can find happiness and enjoyment from within.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>You&rsquo;ll also learn that Jester&rsquo;s can connect with others without starting to become, dare we say it, dull or annoying (when they take the joke too far). There really is no need for the Jester to jeopardize their ability to attain a sense of enjoyment or connection - they just need to learn how to do it in a way that serves them well.</p>
