            <div class="step3-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Sense of Significance</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/sun-glow.png" style="filter:none">                
                <p>Attaining a sense of significance is a vital need for everybody.If we don&rsquo;t figure out a way to feel significant, we can start to become stagnant, we might develop poor confidence, and our well-being begins to deplete.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Most people naturally figure out a way to develop their sense of significance, and in the case ofThe Jester Archetype, they attain their significance through their sense of humor.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If a Jester cannot make somebody smile and have fun, they are in their element.If the Jester is not having fun, then things quickly become irrelevant, tedious and boring to them.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>As you have probably already considered, life is not fun all of the time which is a grave problem for the Jester.If they are not enjoying something, they feel insignificant and unworthy, and so they create enjoyment to chase the sense of significance they desire.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s a vicious circle.</p>
                <p>What Jesters don&rsquo;t realize though, is that if they were to take a more in-depth look at themselves, and how they experience life, they could achieve a sense of significance that stays with them all of the time rather than having to chase it or work for it regularly.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>All they have to do is learn how to live joyfully, instead of superficially attaining some fun and enjoyment at varying levels of success and sometimes at the cost of friendships, lovers and a balanced and fulfilled life.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Since the Jester seeks to connect through happiness and enjoyment, they are often not deeply happy permanently - instead attaining happiness is something to strive for.But it only takes a few tweaks and courageous steps to find the joy and connection that Jesters are capable of experiencing and that will stay with them forever.</p>
                <div class="prev-next">
                    <div class="container">
                        <div class="row mx-auto col-reverse">
                            <div class="col-sm-6 mx-auto">
                                <button class="btn step2-back hover f-left">2. Unique Contribution</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-sm-6">
                                <button class="btn step4 hover f-right">4. Personality Traits</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step4-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Personality Traits</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/floral.png">
                <p>The Jester archetype is the typical life and soul of the party; they are usually extremely popular in social situations because they are often hilariously funny and hugely entertaining.</p>
                <p>If you have a Jester in your circle of friends, you can be sure that there has been plenty of laughter and fun.</p>
                <p><strong>When The Party Ends</strong></p>
                <p>Unfortunately, though, that&rsquo;s pretty much where it stops for most Jesters. Their need for connection through enjoyment and their fear of mediocrity keeps them locked in this space meaning that they often don't show any depth of character, and sometimes don&rsquo;t seem to take life seriously at all.Which can be annoying when there are pressing matters at hand, where jokes are not necessary and sometimes even considered rude.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Eventually, the fun times have to end, but not for the Jester.So, after a while, the fun stops being fun. Ultimately, the joke becomes annoying and well, sorry to say dear Jesters but irrelevant and boring.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Irrelevant and boring is the last thing that a Jester wants to be, in fact, they fear irrelevancy. And if they have reached the realization that they could be irrelevant, it will not be lost on the Jester. They will take in the rejection, and it will hurt them deeply.Of course, they will counter this with more jokes and fun times, while they&rsquo;re dying inside.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This cycle continues to spiral downwards in the worst cases unless the Jester starts to correct their patterns and can find a balance between their jokes and serious matters.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>In many situations though, the Jesters will have already begun to learn how to adjust their natural tendencies to joke things off. Otherwise, as we&rsquo;ve previously discussed, they won&rsquo;t manage to live a normal life successfully &ndash; not if they make everything a joke, and avoid the mundane aspects of life.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The Jester has the potential to be the true life and soul of the party and also to manage to have a fun and fulfilling life - what a wonderful life it would be.But to step into their power, Jesters first need to sort out the issues that they have that hold them back.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Why Do We Hide Ourselves Even From Ourselves?</strong></p>
                <p>Every person has a hidden side.Jung calls it a shadow aspect, and it&rsquo;s discussed in great detail in our Premium Archetype Reports.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Here at Individuologist.com we realize that there is a hidden side or an unconscious world (to be more precise) that we experience internally, but we don&rsquo;t, or can't show or express this existence outwardly.It&rsquo;s this hidden aspect that can bring about great reward if we were to focus our attention on it. It&rsquo;s also crucial for helping each different archetype overcome their greatest challenge.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Before we get started, it&rsquo;s important to acknowledge that there&rsquo;s also a hidden part of us that remains unconscious even to ourselves too and the process of individuation can help us to uncover these hidden aspects of our &lsquo;self&rsquo; too.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>When we start to uncover these &lsquo;hidden&rsquo; aspects of our &lsquo;self,&rsquo; we begin to learn about what is really driving us.We discover the reasons why we do the things we do (or don&rsquo;t do the things that we want to do, or should do).This gives us the opportunity to start to consciously reconcile these hidden aspects so that we can achieve our deepest desires or reach our fullest potential.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Irrelevancy Is Terrifying</strong></p>
                <p>The Jester is terrified of being irrelevant, mundane or bored.If they haven&rsquo;t already made some changes in how they live, then at their extreme, the Jester would find all normal daily activities a drag more so than any other archetype.And while some Jesters&rsquo; will have learned to deal with the boredom of daily life, others may find it difficult to maintain routine and good habits. This could eventually lead them to sabotaging their own lives in the quest for fun.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Of course, this is the most extreme example of the challenges that a Jester faces, and as we live life, we often learn how to counter some of these issues naturally or through our schooling or parenting. Fortunately, many Jesters manage to achieve this.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>However, the Jester may not have fully attained a deep sense of joy, and they may not have relinquished their fear of being irrelevant or boring at this stage, even if they have learned to balance out their lives.Instead, they may have just accepted that they have to do things that they don&rsquo;t enjoy.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>In this case, the fear of being irrelevant will lie in the shadows of the Jester until such a time when they decide to face it. As a matter of fact, this fear that can be the cause of insecurity, a lack of confidence or esteem, and even depression.But this is also something that the Jester probably won&rsquo;t express to others.Instead when they are dying inside - even if they are sad all of the time, they will continue to joke around and create fun for others.</p>
                <p>You often hear cases of comedians making people laugh but being deeply depressed behind closed doors, entertainers and showmen often have the same experiences as comedians also.There&rsquo;s the classic image that we have all probably seen of the clown with tears pouring down his face.This is how life could be for a Jester if they allow it to be.However, it doesn&rsquo;t have to be that way at all.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It just takes for the Jester to look into the shadows of his or her soul, and understand what it is that they are craving, crying over, or feeling unfulfilled about.They can then begin to learn how to reconcile and heal these problems, and it&rsquo;s this process that can take a sad clown and turn it into the most wonderful entertainer and showman (or woman) who also feels immense joy in their heart and soul too.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It might not seem as though that is possible for some Jesters, but the potential to achieve this is closer than you think.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It is your destiny to feel the wonders that real joy can bring but to attain this experience you must first overcome the hurdles that are preventing you from getting there, and you can do so through the process of individuation and also shadow work.&nbsp;</p>
