            <div class="step6-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Greatest Challenge</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/success.png">
                <p>The greatest challenge that the Jester Archetype faces is to learn how to attain a sense of joy in all things.  Rather than achieving a sense of ‘happiness’ in a fleeting moment that never lasts and rarely reaches the heart and soul of the Jester.</p>
                <p>That’s a big statement, even if it doesn’t seem as though it is.  There are a lot of patterns and habits that a Jester would need to concentrate on to attain such joy.  The Jester would also need to develop an understanding of what behavioral and mindset patterns or habits they have that don’t serve them so that they can change them.</p>
                <p>The Jester has smaller issues to fix so that they can attain their deepest desires than most archetypes, but such issues are easier to identify and adjust than other archetypes issues too.</p>
                <p>Here are some of the critical issues that a Jester faces that all add together to build up to the Jester’s greatest challenge.</p>
                <p><strong>The Jester Only Attains A Superficial Sense of Joy</strong></p>
                <p>Jesters need to acknowledge and address their deeper needs rather than just reacting to their superficial needs.Most Jesters probably haven&rsquo;t stopped to look inside to realize that the happiness they seek, is often superficial and never lasts.What they don&rsquo;t understand is that if they were to explore more and seek to understand what they need, they can learn more about how to connect through enjoyment in a way that is deeply fulfilling for them and that they&rsquo;d never have to chase fun and enjoyment ever again.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Sounds too good to be true right?&nbsp;</p>
                <p>But it&rsquo;s easily done and perfectly within the Jesters reach.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Jester&rsquo;s Need to Overcome Their Fear of Being Mundane or Irrelevant.</strong></p>
                <p>To be able to attain the sense of joy that we propose, the Jester needs to face their fears and start to allow themselves to experience what it&rsquo;s like to be mundane or irrelevant occasionally so that they can learn the lessons that are being presented to them through that experience.Lessons such as; patience, self-belief, humility and that they are still ok!If they do this successfully, the Jester will never have to deal with the fear of irrelevancy again.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This means that fear will go away and when it does the joy will start to creep in and prevent you from feeling mundane or irrelevant ever again.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s a contradiction, that&rsquo;s for sure, but one that&rsquo;s well worth paying attention to.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>The Jester Needs to Learn How To Love And Accept Themselves.</strong></p>
                <p>Part of looking inside and understanding why you do the things you do - or don&rsquo;t do the things you should, will assist the Jester in learning how to love and accept themselves so that fears such as the one discussed above never have the opportunity to arise in the first place.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Jester&rsquo;s Would Benefit from Understanding the Difference Between Happiness and Joy</strong></p>
                <p>There&rsquo;s a difference between happiness and joy. Happiness is an experience of joy or satisfaction that occurs in a fleeting moment.Joy lasts and can become permanent.You can even feel joyful while you are feeling bored.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Yes, dear Jester, we realize this might not seem real to you, but it is entirely possible.If you can learn how to attain and maintain deep joy, it will never leave your side and will be with you in everything you do.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Jesters Need to Stop Overthinking or Start Paying Attention To How They Think</strong></p>
                <p>Jesters don&rsquo;t help themselves because they often overthink, become nervous or overreact to things and then when they realize what they are doing, they will adjust or cover their actions with some comedic act.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Which means that people often don&rsquo;t take the Jester serious.This pattern can also cause lots of problems in a Jester&rsquo;s life that will take away the happiness they work so hard for.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Some Jesters may have developed a coping strategy to counter this problem of overthinking whereby they switch themselves off and don&rsquo;t pay attention to the things they probably should, and instead, they seem to naturally hit the default &lsquo;laugh it off&rsquo; response to pretty much anything.</p>
                <p>The outcome in either example won&rsquo;t contribute to a strong sense of self, significance or joy because of the reaction or effects of their actions will result in further rejection.</p>
                <p>The sad thing is Jesters don&rsquo;t mean for this to happen at all, it just does and can sabotage their self-esteem, confidence and even trust in themselves!If they can address this though, they can start to address their greatest challenge.</p>
                <p><strong>Jesters Often Don&rsquo;t Realize They Have The Tools To Attain Joy.</strong></p>
                <p>Jesters probably misuse their gifts, mostly because of having low esteem and a learned pattern of behavior that encourages the Jester to use their skills in the way that they are accustomed too (usually involving only looking for fun times).&nbsp;</p>
                <p>They often don&rsquo;t realize that with a little bit of foresight and effort that these same tools, in the way that they are using them are sabotaging them.But if they learned how to use them well, then they become their secret weapon and bringer of real joy!&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>The Jester Needs to Master Routine and Mediocracy To Attain Joy.</strong></p>
                <p>Learning how to find joy in the most mundane situations is a crucial lesson for the Jester, if they master this then they manage to whip their life into shape in a way that they have never been able to do before.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Which means more confidence, esteem, and self-trust, which are all required to attain a sense of joy.</p>
                <p><strong>How The Jester Archetype Can Master Their Greatest Challenge</strong></p>
                <p>The Jester needs to pay attention to the points highlighted above and start to build habits, patterns, and beliefs to correct and align themselves with what they truly desire and need - joy and connection.</p>
                <p>If they don&rsquo;t, they find that they only end up with fleeting moments of happiness and a deep sense of sadness and disconnection inside and it doesn&rsquo;t have to be this way.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The process of individuation is a wonderful tool that will help the Jester to start to use their intelligence and funny bone in all the right places and to clear up any issues that are preventing them from feeling joy.Shadow work, in particular, is an integral part of this process and you can learn more about this in the Premium Archetype Reports.</p>
